          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "ms2v8l1h5j3g50k8",
          "message": {
            "text": "The scan is deliberately whole-file — no skipping of HTML comments or fenced code blocks — because Starlight renders all three.\n\nThe markers this gate exists to catch were spread across exactly those surfaces: prose ((KF-174) after a module link), a table header cell, and a mid-sentence reference. A tokenizer that only looked at prose would have missed several of them, and the false-positive cost of the whole-file rule is zero: a published doc has no legitimate reason to contain KF-<digits> at all.\n\nScope pairs with the exported sync map (0): source docs come from MAP, and everything under site/src/content/docs/ is walked directly so hand-authored site pages (which never pass through the sync script) are covered too.\n",
            "markdown": "The scan is deliberately whole-file — no skipping of HTML comments or fenced code blocks — because Starlight renders all three.\n\nThe markers this gate exists to catch were spread across exactly those surfaces: prose (`(KF-174)` after a module link), a table header cell, and a mid-sentence reference. A tokenizer that only looked at prose would have missed several of them, and the false-positive cost of the whole-file rule is zero: a published doc has no legitimate reason to contain `KF-<digits>` at all.\n\nScope pairs with [the exported sync map](0): source docs come from `MAP`, and everything under `site/src/content/docs/` is walked directly so hand-authored site pages (which never pass through the sync script) are covered too.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check-doc-site-tickets.mjs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 60,
                  "endLine": 68,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "}\n\nfunction findMarkers(path) {\n  const hits = [];\n  const lines = readFileSync(path, 'utf8').split('\\n');\n  lines.forEach((line, i) => {\n    const found = line.match(TICKET_RE);\n    if (found) hits.push({ line: i + 1, text: line.trim(), markers: [...new Set(found)] });\n  });"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
